    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Change: Reject duplicate normalized telephone with 409\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint already normalizes the submitted telephone (strips non-digits, requires exactly 10 digits). I added a uniqueness check on top of that:\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` (`rest/advice/`), carrying the offending normalized telephone.\n\n2. **Controller guard** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 after `normalizeTelephone(...)`, a new `rejectDuplicateTelephone(...)` step compares the normalized telephone against every existing owner's telephone (each normalized the same way \u2014 digits only), throwing the exception on a match.\n\n3. **Exception handler** (`ExceptionControllerAdvice`) \u2014 maps `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` to **409 Conflict** with a `ProblemDetail` body whose `errors` array names `telephone`, mirroring the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400) handler.\n\nBecause comparison is done on stripped digits for both the incoming value and stored values, it matches regardless of formatting differences in stored data.\n\n**Test results:** the full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` (expects 409) and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` (expects 2xx) both pass; `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
